Since we have AI, bosses shouldn't defeat me simply by having a huge health pool and much stronger abilities than mine. They should beat me through strategic mind games. For example, a boss could cancel an ability's wind-up to trick me. We need to think carefully about the skill design and study how other games handle this. We should also consider cooperation with my companion. As a starting point, perhaps I could be a warrior while the boss is a mage, or vice versa. The boss could also learn and adapt, forcing us to coordinate in order to defeat it. Right now, companions seem to be ignored by enemies. The boss should be able to choose which target it considers worth attacking, creating more strategic possibilities.
